MID_SC00_06_m01: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m01_001: Hmm, I remember you. That time you appeared out\nof nowhere before me...
MID_SC00_06_m01_002: Why were you there? Why are you here? For some\nreason, I cannot fathom, you make me furious...
MID_SC00_06_m02: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m02_001: Hmm? Those strange outfits and martial arts... You're\nthe last of the People of the White Egg, aren't you?
MID_SC00_06_m03: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m03_001: Grrr... So you can put up...a bit of a fight...
MID_SC00_06_m04: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m04_001: I should have seen this coming. I just didn't think\nhe'd draw on the power of the underworld to do it.
MID_SC00_06_m04_002: This won't be as simple as last time. We can't use\nArtemis underground.
MID_SC00_06_m04_003: Is it really up to us few to deal with an enemy of\nhis magnitude?
MID_SC00_06_m17: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m04_004: I was right to think our numbers weren't enough\nfor this fight.
MID_SC00_06_m05: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m05_001: It's already started? Someone's fighting a\nhuge dragon!
MID_SC00_06_m18: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m05_002: Hmph. Am I late to arrive? Regardless, the queen\nof Saramis has come to your aid.
MID_SC00_06_m19: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m05_003: Seems there's no need for a long talk about strategy.\nWe just take that thing down.
MID_SC00_06_m15: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m15_001: That white-clad figure... It couldn't be!
MID_SC00_06_m20: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m15_002: The infernal beast draws me in...my pulse pounds at\nthe sight of it. It has been too long.
MID_SC00_06_m21: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m15_003: Know this, evil spirit. You are an infestation—a\ndisease. On my honor as Mediator, I will undo you!
MID_SC00_06_m16: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m16_001: The fighting has already started? I must do my\npart!
MID_SC00_06_m22: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m16_002: Am I late to the party? Everyone knows the real star\nis always last to arrive.
MID_SC00_06_m06: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m06_001: It's folly to think you can best me. I'll send every last\none of you to the underworld!
MID_SC00_06_m07: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m07_001: I've been waiting. And I haven't forgotten the pact\nwe made.
MID_SC00_06_m07_002: I'm with you. You can count on me.
MID_SC00_06_m08: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m08_001: I see that you kept your promise. I have awaited you.
MID_SC00_06_m08_002: You have attracted a compelling opponent. I can let\nloose my full strength upon it!
MID_SC00_06_m09: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m09_001: I have come to honor the promise I made to you\nyears ago.
MID_SC00_06_m09_002: We have long awaited the day when a beacon for the\ncounterattack would rise somewhere in the world.
MID_SC00_06_m10: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_m10_001: I know I owe you for everything. I came here today\nto pay you back.
MID_SC00_06_m10_002: It's good to see you after all this time.
MID_SC00_06_m11: 
MID_SC00_06_m11_001: 
MID_SC00_06_m11_002: 
MID_SC00_06_m12: 
MID_SC00_06_m12_001: 
MID_SC00_06_m12_002: 
MID_SC00_06_m13: 
MID_SC00_06_m13_001: 
MID_SC00_06_m13_002: 
MID_SC00_06_m14: 
MID_SC00_06_m14_001: 
MID_SC00_06_m14_002: 
MID_SC00_06_e02: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_e02_001: So much miasma...and it sticks to you too.
MID_SC00_06_e02_002: It's clearly a ploy to {SetColor=Gold}hinder our attacks{SetColor=Default}. Be careful,\neveryone!
MID_SC00_06_e03: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_e03_001: We're surrounded. I should have known this wouldn't\nbe easy.
MID_SC00_06_e04: <TH>
MID_SC00_06_e04_001: You fool! This is why I harped on about it being\nimpossible without the Flame Lords!
MID_SC00_06_e04_002: I'll do you the favor of using my power to return us to\nthe Obelisk Chamber. Think before setting out again!
MID_SC00_07_m01: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m01_001: You. You're the welp who ruined my paradise. I will\nnever forget you. And I will never forgive you!
MID_SC00_07_m01_002: Huh. The old man's greed didn't die with him.
MID_SC00_07_m02: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m02_001: I'll paint you into the afterlife!
MID_SC00_07_m03: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m03_001: It's you... The woman who took everything from me!
MID_SC00_07_m03_002: This is uncomfortable. If you expect an apology for\nmy taking vengeance, you'll be disappointed.
MID_SC00_07_m04: 
MID_SC00_07_m04_001: 
MID_SC00_07_m04_002: 
MID_SC00_07_m05: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m05_001: This is my territory. Mine! How dare you\nencroach here...
MID_SC00_07_m06: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m06_001: What are you doing, Nathan? Why aren't you killing\nmy enemies for me?
MID_SC00_07_m06_002: I've gotten used to killing people I knew in life. This,\nhowever...I was not prepared for.
MID_SC00_07_m07: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m07_001: Why, Creek? Have even you betrayed me?
MID_SC00_07_m07_002: My actions may not have been what you expected,\nbut to call them a "betrayal"? You wound me.
MID_SC00_07_m08: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m08_001: Now's my chance to curry some favor with Balor!
MID_SC00_07_m09: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m09_001: Sweetie, you're just like you used to be... Beautiful,\neven in death.
MID_SC00_07_m09_002: Really, all I wanted— Oh... All I wanted was for you\nto be with me.
MID_SC00_07_m10: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m10_001: Show me your strength!
MID_SC00_07_m11: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m11_001: I've waited so long to cross blades with you,\nthe one they call a savior.
MID_SC00_07_m11_002: Let's see if you can save yourself!
MID_SC00_07_m12: 
MID_SC00_07_m12_001: 
MID_SC00_07_m12_002: 
MID_SC00_07_m13: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m13_001: You and I are cut from the same cloth, foreigner.\nWe both crave battle above all else!
MID_SC00_07_m13_002: We do. We should test each other to see how we\nmatch...and how we differ.
MID_SC00_07_m14: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_m14_001: Now, come! Why waste time talking, when we could\nbe fighting?
MID_SC00_07_e01: <TH>
MID_SC00_07_e01_001: The miasma covering this place seems even more\nsinister than the last.
MID_SC00_07_e01_002: I suspect it will {SetColor=Gold}sap our vitality{SetColor=Default}. We would do well to\navoid touching it.
MID_SC00_13_m01: <TH>
MID_SC00_13_m01_001: Urghhh... Must...eliminate...the enemy.
MID_SC00_13_m01_002: It's so hard to see you like this, Anatolia...
MID_SC00_13_m01_003: But I've gotta do what's right.
MID_SC00_13_m02: <TH>
MID_SC00_13_m02_001: Urrrgh... Dadao...
MID_SC00_13_m02_002: I'm sorry, Anatolia. I have to do this.
MID_SC00_13_m03: <TH>
MID_SC00_13_m03_001: I need you to know, Toli... I'll always remember the\nday you saved me.
MID_SC00_13_m03_002: Ahhhrgh...
MID_SC00_13_m04: <TH>
MID_SC00_13_m04_001: No one will stand in our way. I will eliminate each\nof you without fail!
MID_SC00_13_m05: <TH>
MID_SC00_13_m05_001: Promised One? Tch. What flattery. You're simply\na delusional mess, siding with the beasts.
MID_SC00_13_m05_002: If you lived up to your title, you'd have saved us!
MID_SC00_13_m06: 
MID_SC00_13_m06_001: 
MID_SC00_13_m06_002: 
MID_SC00_13_m07: 
MID_SC00_13_m07_001: 
MID_SC00_13_m07_002: 
MID_SC00_13_m08: 
MID_SC00_13_m08_001: 
MID_SC00_13_m08_002: 
MID_SC00_13_m09: <TH>
MID_SC00_13_m09_001: Capable of discourse? Then you have the sense to\ndesist. There is no place in this world for ghosts.
MID_SC00_13_m09_002: You cannot stop our advance.
MID_SC00_13_m10: <TH>
MID_SC00_13_m10_001: Hideous beasts, running freely through our world!
MID_SC00_13_e01: <TH>
MID_SC00_13_e01_001: The miasma here has quite the odor. It smells of\nsome sort of corrosive acid.
MID_SC00_13_e01_002: It {SetColor=Gold}eats away not only weapons but magic too{SetColor=Default}!\nTake care not to be left defenseless!
MID_SC00_08_m01: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_m01_001: Another foe stands across me. I will defeat you,\nand them, and everyone!
MID_SC00_08_m01_002: Bertrand... Goodbye. I'll survive for you.
MID_SC00_08_m02: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_m02_001: You will not see tomorrow, whoever you are.
MID_SC00_08_m02_002: Brother, I hate you bein' like this. It's hard to watch.
MID_SC00_08_m03: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_m03_001: I can think of no more tragic end to your story\nthan this.
MID_SC00_08_m03_002: Rrgh...
MID_SC00_08_m03_003: That's alright—no need to speak. I can work out your\ndialogue later.
MID_SC00_08_m04: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_m04_001: I will destroy everything... Everything!
MID_SC00_08_m05: 
MID_SC00_08_m05_001: 
MID_SC00_08_m05_002: 
MID_SC00_08_m06: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_m06_001: Let's see which one of us has better luck.
MID_SC00_08_m07: 
MID_SC00_08_m07_001: 
MID_SC00_08_m07_002: 
MID_SC00_08_m08: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_m08_001: It makes me sick... People acting like bad luck is a\npoint of pride.
MID_SC00_08_m09: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_m09_001: Insolent one who stands before me. It appears you\nare prepared to give your life.
MID_SC00_08_m09_002: His presence is matchless. This is no ordinary man.\nCould he be Arago the Upright?
MID_SC00_08_m10: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_m10_001: Who is foolish enough to challenge me? I, who\ngrasped the title of hero with his own two hands!
MID_SC00_08_m11: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_m11_001: There's one true king, and only one. And I am he!
MID_SC00_08_m11_002: I will kill you, so-called savior, and all the fools who\nwrongly exalt you!
MID_SC00_08_m12: 
MID_SC00_08_m12_001: 
MID_SC00_08_m12_002: 
MID_SC00_08_m13: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_m13_001: Your notion of rulership is loathsome to me.
MID_SC00_08_m13_002: Hold your tongue. You know nothing of leadership,\nyou lowly woman!
MID_SC00_08_m14: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_m14_001: Now, worship the true king. Give me your homage\nof blood!
MID_SC00_08_e01: <TH>
MID_SC00_08_e01_001: We can scarcely {SetColor=Gold}find our foes{SetColor=Default} in this {SetColor=Gold}fog{SetColor=Default}. And worse,\nthat dense {SetColor=Gold}miasma{SetColor=Default} chokes the battlefield.
MID_SC00_08_e01_002: 'Twill inevitably {SetColor=Gold}hamper visibility even further{SetColor=Default}. Take\ncare not to be caught in a surprise attack!
MID_SC00_11_m01: 
MID_SC00_11_m01_001: 
MID_SC00_11_m01_002: 
MID_SC00_11_m02: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_m02_001: I can't let you past. I won't let you do it.
MID_SC00_11_m03: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_m03_001: If I can just...get my hands...on the treasure...
MID_SC00_11_m03_002: That guy? He was with us under Dagsion.
MID_SC00_11_m04: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_m04_001: The treasure... Where is it?
MID_SC00_11_m05: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_m05_001: Buspha... They dragged you into this too.
MID_SC00_11_m05_002: Loretta... Helllp... Help...meee.
MID_SC00_11_m05_003: What am I even supposed to do with all\nTHAT? I can defeat you—that's all!
MID_SC00_11_m06: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_m06_001: Horrible... I am...horrible.
MID_SC00_11_m07: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_m07_001: You, the Promised One... Balor will give me a little\npat on the head if I defeat you!
MID_SC00_11_m07_002: I won't let you run. I will serve you up to him on a\nplatter!
MID_SC00_11_m08: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_m08_001: Ya know, even one of the risen dead shouldn't be\nsuch a jerk.
MID_SC00_11_m08_002: You little brat. I'm going to make you bleed.
MID_SC00_11_m09: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_m09_001: If you are strong, I may recall you once our\nblades clash...
MID_SC00_11_m09_002: You! It's all your fault! Once you showed up, it all\nwent belly-up for me!
MID_SC00_11_m10: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_m10_001: I'll hollow out your corpse and use it as\nan automaton!
MID_SC00_11_e01: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_e01_001: This {SetColor=Gold}miasma{SetColor=Default} is strange... Through its tendrils, our\nfoes appear distorted, or don't appear at all.
MID_SC00_11_e01_002: Are they bending causality? How odd...{SetColor=Gold}some enemies\nmay be harder to hit than others{SetColor=Default}. Be on your guard.
MID_SC00_11_e02: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_e02_001: Is he creating golems as puppets under his control?\nThat Brimstone Lord is quite skilled.
MID_SC00_11_e02_002: That vicious smile he wears suggests he has a trick\nup his sleeve. Watch our enemy's movements closely!
MID_SC00_11_e03: <TH>
MID_SC00_11_e03_001: The real fun starts now! Automata—show them how\nbad things can get!
MID_SC00_09_m01: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_m01_001: I have not forgotten all that you did for me when\nyou were among the living.
MID_SC00_09_m01_002: So...what? You're not giving me your soul as thanks,\nare you?
MID_SC00_09_m01_003: I am not. My soul will not be sold so cheaply as that.
MID_SC00_09_m02: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_m02_001: Here's one ticket to the underworld, free of charge!
MID_SC00_09_m03: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_m03_001: Fatima, is that you?
MID_SC00_09_m03_002: Brother, please... I don't know how else to help\nyou now.
MID_SC00_09_m04: 
MID_SC00_09_m04_001: 
MID_SC00_09_m04_002: 
MID_SC00_09_m05: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_m05_001: You betray me as well, Nathan?
MID_SC00_09_m05_002: Forgive me, my king. My cause is weightier than\npersonal loyalty!
MID_SC00_09_m06: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_m06_001: Do not come any closer... The throne of Arago\nbelongs to me.
MID_SC00_09_m07: 
MID_SC00_09_m07_001: 
MID_SC00_09_m07_002: 
MID_SC00_09_m08: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_m08_001: Where is the mystery in this? Where is the sense\nof grand adventure?
MID_SC00_09_m09: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_m09_001: When I look at you, I feel a phantom twinge in the\narm you cut from me.
MID_SC00_09_m09_002: So, then. You still live. Hurry and join me...
MID_SC00_09_m10: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_m10_001: I AM the demon god Balor. Death to all who\noppose me!
MID_SC00_09_m11: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_m11_001: Another one who thinks they have a claim to\nmy treasure.
MID_SC00_09_m11_002: Well, stay away! Every coin, every jewel, every\nkeepsake—it's all MINE!
MID_SC00_09_m12: 
MID_SC00_09_m12_001: 
MID_SC00_09_m12_002: 
MID_SC00_09_m13: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_m13_001: Hey, if I beat you, I get your money, right?
MID_SC00_09_m13_002: The hell you say! No one will get their greasy paws\non my treasure!
MID_SC00_09_m14: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_m14_001: Drop those treasures and leave—if you value\nyour life!
MID_SC00_09_e01: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_e01_001: Oh? I sense no miasma on this battlefield. We may\ngo where we please, for once!
MID_SC00_09_e01_002: Though I still have the odd sense that 'twould be\nunwise to let our guard down...
MID_SC00_09_e02: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_e02_001: Aah! Defeating their soldiers caused miasma to\nspew forth? I knew 'twas too good to be true...
MID_SC00_09_e02_002: This pernicious miasma can {SetColor=Gold}confuse the senses {SetColor=Default}of\nfriend and foe alike. Stay on your guard!
MID_SC00_09_e03: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_e03_001: By the way, have you noticed the {SetColor=Gold}shiny things{SetColor=Default}\nscattered about the area?
MID_SC00_09_e03_002: Do you suppose they're treasures pilfered by the\nrisen dead? Wretched things.
MID_SC00_09_e03_003: They emit a strange energy... I suspect that {SetColor=Gold}whoever\npossesses{SetColor=Default} one {SetColor=Gold}is immune to the miasma{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC00_09_e04: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_e04_001: Oho... It seems {SetColor=Gold}whoever possesses the Pirate King's\ntreasure {SetColor=Default}is {SetColor=Gold}immune to the miasma{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC00_09_e04_002: It must be attuned to displays of wealth. Whatever\nthe reason, we can use this to our advantage!
MID_SC00_09_e05: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_e05_001: Those wretched risen dead are hoarding the treasure!\nLet's seize it back for the benefit of the living.
MID_SC00_09_e06: <TH>
MID_SC00_09_e06_001: {SetColor=Gold}Whoever possesses{SetColor=Default} these {SetColor=Gold}is immune to the miasma{SetColor=Default}.\nWe should collect more before engaging the enemy.
MID_SC00_10_m01: <TH>
MID_SC00_10_m01_001: Who dares stand in the way of my dream? I shall\ncrush them...destroy them utterly...
MID_SC00_10_m01_002: Poor Theodora... Have you forgotten even me?
MID_SC00_10_m02: <TH>
MID_SC00_10_m02_001: You could never understand the depths of the\ngrudge we bear...
MID_SC00_10_m03: <TH>
MID_SC00_10_m03_001: Is that you, my dear sister? Don't you remember...
MID_SC00_10_m03_002: Even you have found yourself in Balor's clutches...\nI will put you to rest right away, my brother.
MID_SC00_10_m04: <TH>
MID_SC00_10_m04_001: I wanted everything...but I couldn't keep hold\nof anything...
MID_SC00_10_m05: <TH>
MID_SC00_10_m05_001: "Promised One," was it? You are better than I\nassumed you'd be.
MID_SC00_10_m05_002: But whose power is greater, yours or mine? Let us\nput that to the test.
MID_SC00_10_m06: <TH>
MID_SC00_10_m06_001: You should know that it was because of you that I\nsaw my own ambitions realized.
MID_SC00_10_m06_002: As a proud warrior of your lineage, I owe it to you\nto meet you blow for blow in battle.
MID_SC00_10_m07: <TH>
MID_SC00_10_m07_001: Whoa, you're Mahadu! Damn, who'd have thought\nI'd be facing off against you?
MID_SC00_10_m07_002: Even if you're a Brimstone Lord now, you're still the\nguy I've looked up to ever since I was a kid!
MID_SC00_10_m08: <TH>
MID_SC00_10_m08_001: What was our crime? What did Damascar ever do\nto Dagda the Great?
MID_SC00_10_e01: <TH>
MID_SC00_10_e01_001: Oho... The miasma here is brimming with the power\nof brave warriors who fell to the underworld.
MID_SC00_10_e01_002: That {SetColor=Gold}power could be ours{SetColor=Default} if we stand within it,\nbut 'twould be a {SetColor=Gold}double-edged sword{SetColor=Default}. Be careful.
MID_SC00_10_e02: <TH>
MID_SC00_10_e02_001: I sense that they have troops in reserve. Mind that\nyou don't fall apart when reinforcements arrive.
MID_SC00_12_m01: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m01_001: Now, let's show them our power! Shall we, Maria?
MID_SC00_12_m01_002: Yes, my dear...
MID_SC00_12_m02: 
MID_SC00_12_m02_001: 
MID_SC00_12_m02_002: 
MID_SC00_12_m02_003: 
MID_SC00_12_m02_004: 
MID_SC00_12_m03: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m03_001: Who's looking to die? Have at me!
MID_SC00_12_m04: 
MID_SC00_12_m04_001: 
MID_SC00_12_m04_002: 
MID_SC00_12_m05: 
MID_SC00_12_m05_001: 
MID_SC00_12_m05_002: 
MID_SC00_12_m05_003: 
MID_SC00_12_m06: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m06_001: Everything we did, it was for Father.
MID_SC00_12_m07: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m07_001: Leilidahna, is that you?
MID_SC00_12_m07_002: Father Mahdel... If I told you back then that I\nforgave you, would you have turned out like this?
MID_SC00_12_m07_003: Would your soul still have been ensnared by the\nunderworld?
MID_SC00_12_m08: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m08_001: I... I'm...
MID_SC00_12_m09: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m09_001: A-aaah...
MID_SC00_12_m09_002: Father... There's no place in your heart for Leilidahna\nanymore. Is there?
MID_SC00_12_m10: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m10_001: Enemy of Balor. You will not escape.
MID_SC00_12_m11: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m11_001: You... You're the reason I'm...
MID_SC00_12_m11_002: Another face I hoped I'd never see again.
MID_SC00_12_m11_003: I don't care about being resented. I stopped caring\nthe day I swore to take my revenge.
MID_SC00_12_m12: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m12_001: Rrrgh! Die!
MID_SC00_12_m13: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m13_001: So you've come! Let's begin, shall we?
MID_SC00_12_m13_002: I'll play a song to celebrate the savior's death—\nand the end of this cruel world!
MID_SC00_12_m14: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m14_001: Take your place by my side! Let us perform the\nmelody of heaven and earth...
MID_SC00_12_m14_002: Thanks for the offer. But I'm not interested in a duet\nwith a dead man.
MID_SC00_12_m15: 
MID_SC00_12_m15_001: 
MID_SC00_12_m15_002: 
MID_SC00_12_m15_003: 
MID_SC00_12_m16: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m16_001: Beautiful! Won't you come to me, darling?
MID_SC00_12_m16_002: Considering your legendary genius, I find your\ninterest in me quite flattering! But no.
MID_SC00_12_m16_003: I have hundreds—thousands—of masterpieces left\nto write. I can't go to the underworld now!
MID_SC00_12_m17: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_m17_001: Now, by the beautiful tune of my melody, you shall\nbe carried to the underworld...
MID_SC00_12_e01: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_e01_001: This miasma feels incredibly vile. No doubt 'tis\nimbued with some bewitching power.
MID_SC00_12_e01_002: Remain in it, and it will {SetColor=Gold}cloud your ability to perceive\nthe enemy{SetColor=Default}. Take care not to fall under its spell!
MID_SC00_12_e02: <TH>
MID_SC00_12_e02_001: The miasma has drifted?! He'll stop at nothing until\nwe are all bewitched.
MID_SC00_14_m01: <TH>
MID_SC00_14_m01_001: You will not go any farther. Do not interfere in\nFather's plans. I will not permit it.
MID_SC00_14_m02: <TH>
MID_SC00_14_m02_001: Tch... Can I go no further?
MID_SC00_14_m03: <TH>
MID_SC00_14_m03_001: I suppose I must admit that I am impressed. You\nhave forced a change in my tactics.
MID_SC00_14_m03_002: Come forth, fiercest soldiers of the underworld! Bring\nterror to those foolish enough to oppose your king!
MID_SC00_14_m04: <TH>
MID_SC00_14_m04_001: I still do not comprehend your nature,\nPromised One...
MID_SC00_14_m04_002: But it does not matter. I will bring an end to you here\nand now, and that will settle the question you pose!
MID_SC00_14_m05: 
MID_SC00_14_m05_001: 
MID_SC00_14_m05_002: 
MID_SC00_14_m05_003: 
MID_SC00_14_m05_004: 
MID_SC00_14_m06: <TH>
MID_SC00_14_m06_001: Dietrich...
MID_SC00_14_m06_002: You look so sad, but your wish came true, did it not?\nYou should be glad of it.
MID_SC00_14_m06_003: I only think that, had I been born under different\ncircumstances...I'd be at your side now.
MID_SC00_14_m06_004: What is past is past. And now, it is time.
MID_SC00_14_m07: <TH>
MID_SC00_14_m07_001: I don't understand, Magistra Raksha. Why would you\nprotect this place?!
MID_SC00_14_m07_002: I would have thought it obvious. It is for my father.\nAs I am his daughter, it falls to me!
MID_SC00_14_m08: <TH>
MID_SC00_14_m08_001: Now...I will teach each and every one of you the\ntrue meaning of fear.
MID_SC00_14_e01: <TH>
MID_SC00_14_e01_001: 'Tis scattering all over the place. Is that their plan?\nTo {SetColor=Gold}spread the miasma as they move{SetColor=Default}?
MID_SC00_14_e01_002: And that smell...it's paralyzing. Stay alert! She aims\nto {SetColor=Gold}sap our ability to fight{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC00_15_m01: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m01_001: Did you think you could corner me so easily? I am\nBalor, not some mewling mortal!
MID_SC00_15_m01_002: Ludicrous "Promised One," behold my power!
MID_SC00_15_m02: 
MID_SC00_15_m02_001: 
MID_SC00_15_m02_002: 
MID_SC00_15_m03: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m03_001: I will show you the folly of defying me in the\nunderworld.
MID_SC00_15_m04: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m04_001: For the world of humans, and to reclaim the light,\nI won't falter.
MID_SC00_15_m05: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m05_001: Just you watch, Great-Grandpa. I won't lose.
MID_SC00_15_m06: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m06_001: Balor! Push me to the distant heights that lie beyond\nall joy!
MID_SC00_15_m07: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m07_001: I shall win victory for Saramis, and for all the nations\nof humanity!
MID_SC00_15_m08: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m08_001: Leave it to a man to be so strongheaded he ends the\nwhole world.
MID_SC00_15_m08_002: Well, fine... We'll cut your stubbornness out of you.
MID_SC00_15_m09: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m09_001: Twisted god. Your reign of oppression and cruelty\ncomes to an end today.
MID_SC00_15_m10: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m10_001: To still hate the world after thousands of years...\nGotta say, I see where I get my resolve.
MID_SC00_15_m10_002: But I guess that means it's up to me to free you from\nthat hate, eh, Gramps?
MID_SC00_15_m11: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m11_001: My words have failed to persuade you. You've left\nme no other choice. I'll force you to listen!
MID_SC00_15_m12: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m12_001: We'll end this war here and weave a future for the\nworld of the living.
MID_SC00_15_m13: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m13_001: I may be standing witness to a monumental\nhistorical event for the land of Dagda.
MID_SC00_15_m13_002: I won't die and leave my name to historians. I will\nreturn alive and write the story myself.
MID_SC00_15_m14: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m14_001: I don't understand why Balor would do such\nterrible things.
MID_SC00_15_m14_002: But many people are suffering, and I can't let\nthat stand.
MID_SC00_15_m15: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m15_001: He might be Aurora's grandfather, but wrong\nis wrong.
MID_SC00_15_m16: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m16_001: I can't let my fear take over. We're fighting for the\nfuture of humanity!
MID_SC00_15_m17: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m17_001: You know what? I feel good about this. We're gonna\nmake it, and we're gonna win!
MID_SC00_15_m17_002: I'll prove everyone wrong about me...and show 'em\ngods aren't so special!
MID_SC00_15_m18: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m18_001: Sometimes, the only way to correct a warped mind\nis with martial prowess.
MID_SC00_15_m19: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m19_001: Thus begins the twilight of a god. One more battle,\nand the morning light shall break through!
MID_SC00_15_m20: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m20_001: When this war ends, so too may my journey. That\nthought is tinged with an unfamiliar sadness.
MID_SC00_15_m21: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m21_001: You might think you're big, Balor, but we'll show\nyou! We can't be put down!
MID_SC00_15_m22: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m22_001: This world belongs to the people who live there now!\nI won't let anybody take that away—not even a god.
MID_SC00_15_m23: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m23_001: For the sake of all people living in this world, we will\nend this here.
MID_SC00_15_m24: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m24_001: Make way for Simon the Sky-Drum! I'm gonna \nenjoy this!
MID_SC00_15_m25: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m25_001: Father...I will fulfill this duty and come back\nhome alive!
MID_SC00_15_m26: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m26_001: For my love, and to make my dreams reality...\nI will not die here.
MID_SC00_15_m27: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m27_001: Balor, god of the Har Hali... I turn my blade\non you. I choose life—my life.
MID_SC00_15_m28: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m28_001: The demon god Balor... That guy's BEYOND scary.\nBut I'm not gonna run—or lose!
MID_SC00_15_m29: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m29_001: Founder Balor, your defeat is at hand. I will banish\nthe darkness from this world.
MID_SC00_15_m29_002: I swear it on my name—Saint Cichol, defender of\nthe Church of Seiros. And protective father.
MID_SC00_15_m30: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m30_001: Pitiable, pitiable Balor... You can rely on me to help\nyou reach where you belong.
MID_SC00_15_m31: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m31_001: The curtain closes on the age of gods, and opens on\nthe age of humanity. A great change is underway.
MID_SC00_15_m32: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m32_001: Can't believe I'm goin' toe to toe with Balor. Might\nas well aim big, I always say!
MID_SC00_15_m33: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m33_001: I'm gonna get home and be happy with my folks,\nand you're not gonna stop me.
MID_SC00_15_m34: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m34_001: I never thought I'd one day face the demon god.\nBut I do not back down from my duty—not ever.
MID_SC00_15_m35: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m35_001: I will be everyone's shield. No one dies today!
MID_SC00_15_m36: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m36_001: The winds of change are blowing... A southeasterly\ngale is here to rouse me and blow you away, Balor.
MID_SC00_15_m37: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m37_001: I'll stand strong... The daughter of Mikaela Redblade\ndoesn't run away!
MID_SC00_15_m38: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m38_001: I am the Blue Rose of Caelus, and today I will help a\nnew era of peace bloom in this world!
MID_SC00_15_m39: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m39_001: Hell yeah! Today is my day. Nothing's gonna\nstop me!
MID_SC00_15_m40: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m40_001: Back in the village, I'd never have imagined I'd take\npart in determining the fate of the world...
MID_SC00_15_m41: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m41_001: Battle's what I do best! Time to show you what it's\nall about!
MID_SC00_15_m42: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m42_001: I've come so far... I've gotta make it back home,\nno matter what!
MID_SC00_15_m43: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m43_001: Unkillable Guzran versus the demon god? This'll\nmake a great story. Trouble is, nobody will buy it.
MID_SC00_15_m44: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m44_001: Though heaven's net is loose, none may slip\nthrough... Your time is up, demon god!
MID_SC00_15_m45: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m45_001: Everything has its turning point. This is yours.
MID_SC00_15_m46: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m46_001: Opposing a frenzied god is but another of a king's\nduties. Gaze well upon our visage!
MID_SC00_15_m47: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m47_001: If we win, then everything will turn out just fine. \nSo we'd better do our best!
MID_SC00_15_m48: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m48_001: Looking pretty scary, Bally. But you won't frighten\nme off.
MID_SC00_15_m49: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m49_001: For my glory—no, for all humanity!—I will smite this\ntyrannical god!
MID_SC00_15_m50: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m50_001: I happen to be fairly attached to this world.
MID_SC00_15_m51: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m51_001: Aah! That thing is huge, and it means business.\nNot good for us!
MID_SC00_15_m52: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m52_001: How in the hell did I get dragged along? I don't\nbelong here!
MID_SC00_15_m53: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m53_001: A battlefield befitting a mighty general, and the best\nchance to deploy my finest tactics. I can't wait!
MID_SC00_15_m54: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m54_001: If we triumph, we'll put an end to all of this. I swear\nI'll do it, Promised One!
MID_SC00_15_m55: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m55_001: I'm a stubborn weed, and I have my pride. I'll give\nyou a taste of my blade, Balor, at least once!
MID_SC00_15_m56: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m56_001: Here we go! It's time to restore the order of the world\nand bring forth the light!
MID_SC00_15_m57: 
MID_SC00_15_m57_001: 
MID_SC00_15_m58: 
MID_SC00_15_m58_001: 
MID_SC00_15_m59: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m59_001: This is it, Promised One. Finish the job for us,\nand for Master Zenon.
MID_SC00_15_m59_002: We're ready to do whatever it takes to help you\nget there, so long as we settle this!
MID_SC00_15_m60: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m60_001: It's not as if Balor has given us reason to show mercy.\nLet us finally quell the chaos!
MID_SC00_15_m61: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m61_001: A battle with the future of humanity on the line... For\na warrior, there is no greater honor!
MID_SC00_15_m62: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m62_001: Balor, the demon god...I will show you just how\ntenacious we humans can be!
MID_SC00_15_m63: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m63_001: Isn't the underworld the den of ghosts? Promised\nOne, let's get this over with and leave!
MID_SC00_15_m64: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m64_001: O great Balor, forgive me for turning my blade\nagainst you!
MID_SC00_15_m65: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m65_001: I know how it is to live a long life, and I'm sure you\nhad your reasons for doing what you did.
MID_SC00_15_m65_002: But I'm a Mediator of Nuwa, and I just can't let you\nget away with it.
MID_SC00_15_m66: 
MID_SC00_15_m66_001: 
MID_SC00_15_m67: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m67_001: I couldn't ask for a better foe than an evil heathen\ngod. Tremble, for a Mosa warrior opposes you!
MID_SC00_15_m68: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_m68_001: With my skills, I can take out anyone—even the lord\nof the underworld!
MID_SC00_15_e01: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_e01_001: That damned Balor... 'Twould seem he's {SetColor=Gold}protected by\na powerful barrier{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC00_15_e02: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_e02_001: I would guess that the gates in this area are the\nreason for it.
MID_SC00_15_e02_002: A direct assault on Balor is impossible for now.\nLet us first {SetColor=Gold}destroy those gates{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC00_15_e04: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_e04_001: Oho...destroying a gate weakened the barrier!
MID_SC00_15_e04_002: Keep {SetColor=Gold}destroying the rest of the gates{SetColor=Default} so that the\nbarrier falls away completely!
MID_SC00_15_e05: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_e05_001: I have a terrible sense that {SetColor=Gold}new gates are appearing{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC00_15_e05_002: They'll be tightening their defenses, but you must\ndestroy them all regardless!
MID_SC00_15_e08: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_e08_001: Your struggles are useless. I will destroy all, and you\nwill not stop me!
MID_SC00_15_e08_002: 'Twould appear we've earned his ire. Look sharp,\nfor the gates here are beginning to roil!
MID_SC00_15_e09: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_e09_001: It can't be... Do I face destruction here...
MID_SC00_15_e13: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_e13_001: He's releasing a tremendous amount of energy into\nthe area!
MID_SC00_15_e13_002: This is the harbinger of some dreadful assault. Take\ncare not to be caught up in it!
MID_SC00_15_e14: <TH>
MID_SC00_15_e14_001: Unfortunately, the barrier protecting Balor seems to\nregenerate if we let up for even a moment.
MID_SC00_15_e14_002: We must rally our forces to press the attack\nimmediately once the barrier is broken!
MID_SC00_16_m01: <TH>
MID_SC00_16_m01_001: This abomination must be destroyed, even if we\nshould fall in the process.
MID_SC00_16_m01_002: This is for the future of all living things!
MID_SC00_16_m02: <TH>
MID_SC00_16_m02_001: You needn't hold back out of any concern for me.
MID_SC00_16_m02_002: My heart is aligned with yours. Now strike, and be\nquick about it!
MID_SC00_16_m03: <TH>
MID_SC00_16_m03_001: Did that one strike true?!
MID_SC00_16_m03_002: Good...the underworld is starting to collapse.\nThis place will soon be swallowed up.
MID_SC00_16_m03_003: Hold on tightly or we'll be separated!
MID_SC00_16_m03_004: Ngh!
MID_DefenseBattle_e01: <TH>
MID_DefenseBattle_e01_001: The cheek of them, coming for us where we are\nstrongest. You! Drive them off and be quick about it!
MID_DefenseBattle_e02: <TH>
MID_DefenseBattle_e02_001: My goodness, they brought reinforcements! Rather\nheinous-looking ones at that.
MID_DefenseBattle_e02_002: {SetColor=Gold}Dagsion will hold{SetColor=Default} even if {SetColor=Gold}we fail it once or twice{SetColor=Default}.\nBut it has its limits, so don't get complacent!
MID_DefenseBattle_e03: <TH>
MID_DefenseBattle_e03_001: Hm? Oh no! The citizens of the capital have been\ncaught in the midst of the fighting!
MID_DefenseBattle_e04: <TH>
MID_DefenseBattle_e04_001: The armies of the underworld crave the blood of the\nliving. If a {SetColor=Gold}citizen falls{SetColor=Default}, it will {SetColor=Gold}give our foes strength{SetColor=Default}!
MID_DefenseBattle_e04_002: Dagsion is nothing without its people. If they fall,\nit will be little use to us as a base.
MID_DefenseBattle_e04_003: Take great pains not to allow all the {SetColor=Gold}citizens{SetColor=Default} to\nbe slain. If they {SetColor=Gold}all fall{SetColor=Default}, we will have {SetColor=Gold}failed{SetColor=Default}!
MID_DefenseBattle_e05: <TH>
MID_DefenseBattle_e05_001: No! A citizen has been slain! The poor thing...
MID_DefenseBattle_e06: <TH>
MID_DefenseBattle_e06_001: 'Tis just as I feared. They've gained even more\nstrength from spilled blood!
MID_DefenseBattle_e06_002: {SetColor=Gold}Allowing citizens to fall{SetColor=Default} will {SetColor=Gold}put us at a disadvantage{SetColor=Default}.\nDon't neglect them as you defeat the risen dead!
MID_DefenseBattle_e07: <TH>
MID_DefenseBattle_e07_001: Without you, our cause is lost. This is a bitter defeat,\nbut we must withdraw.
MID_DefenseBattle_e08: <TH>
MID_DefenseBattle_e08_001: All of the citizens have been slain...'tis a tragedy.\nI see little point in remaining. Let us withdraw.
MID_DefenseBattle_e09: <TH>
MID_DefenseBattle_e09_001: Hmph. Our losses were severe, but the imperial\ncapital still stands defiant!
MID_DefenseBattle_e09_002: Though I wouldn't test its endurance if I were you.\nDon't allow their forces to reach Dagsion again!
MID_DefenseBattle_e10: <TH>
MID_DefenseBattle_e10_001: I can't believe we allowed them to assault the capital\nnot once, but twice!
MID_DefenseBattle_e10_002: Without a base of operations, our campaign against\nBalor is at an end. One more loss is all it would take!
MID_DefenseBattle_e11: <TH>
MID_DefenseBattle_e11_001: Dagsion has fallen... Much as it pains me to admit,\nall is lost...
MID_3_ISM_GameOver_e01: <TH>
MID_3_ISM_GameOver_e01_001: Have you lost all your allies?! This is a disaster!
MID_3_ISM_GameOver_e01_002: 'Tis impossible for anyone, even you, to slay Balor\nalone. I regret to say that our cause is doomed...